{"title":"Career Roadmap: Watershed Officer","role":"Watershed Officer","summary":"Career Domain: Environment, Energy & Sustainability · Qualification Pathway: B.Sc – Soil & Water Conservation / Watershed Management · Target Career: Watershed Officer","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc (Hons) Agriculture and Allied","Course":"Soil & Water Conservation / Watershed Management"},"about":[{"label":"About this roadmap","text":"This roadmap was drafted with AI assistance from OneGrasp's related roadmaps and is awaiting expert review. Check fees, dates, eligibility and exam patterns on the official websites before you rely on them."}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Watershed Officer plans and implements watershed projects - check dams, contour trenches, ponds, tree planting - that save soil and water and raise farm incomes in a whole village area."},{"type":"h","text":"What a Watershed Officer does"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Survey and plan watershed works"},{"text":"Mobilise village committees"},{"text":"Supervise construction and planting"},{"text":"Monitor results and report"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Where they work:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"State watershed and rural development departments (PMKSY-WDC)"},{"text":"NABARD-supported projects"},{"text":"NGOs (e.g. BAIF, WOTR)"},{"text":"Consultancies"}]}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Career stage","Typical role"],"rows":[[{"text":"Entry-level"},{"text":"Watershed Development Officer"}],[{"text":"Early career"},{"text":"Project Officer"}],[{"text":"Mid-level"},{"text":"Project Manager"}],[{"text":"Senior"},{"text":"Programme Head"}],[{"text":"Leadership"},{"text":"State-level Director"}]]}]},{"heading":"Year-by-Year Learning Roadmap","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1: Basics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Soil science and agronomy"},{"text":"Hydrology basics"},{"text":"Visit a watershed project"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2: Soil and water conservation"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Soil and water conservation engineering"},{"text":"Learn GIS for watershed mapping"},{"text":"Community mobilisation basics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3: Field experience"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Intern with a watershed NGO or project"},{"text":"Prepare a micro-watershed plan"},{"text":"Learn MGNREGA and PMKSY works"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 4: Placement"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"RAWE / ELP in a watershed village"},{"text":"Monitoring and evaluation project"},{"text":"Apply to projects and NGOs"}]}]},{"heading":"Essential Skills","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Skill","Type"],"rows":[[{"text":"Watershed planning"},{"text":"Technical"}],[{"text":"Soil and water conservation works"},{"text":"Technical"}],[{"text":"GIS mapping"},{"text":"Technical"}],[{"text":"Monitoring and evaluation"},{"text":"Technical"}],[{"text":"Community mobilisation"},{"text":"Professional"}],[{"text":"Field work"},{"text":"Professional"}],[{"text":"Patience"},{"text":"Professional"}]]}]},{"heading":"Tools and Technologies to Learn","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"QGIS"},{"text":"GPS"},{"text":"Bhuvan (ISRO)"},{"text":"Excel"}]}]},{"heading":"Internships and Practical Experience","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Watershed NGOs"},{"text":"State watershed agencies"},{"text":"NABARD projects"}]}]},{"heading":"Certifications and Additional Training","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"GIS / remote-sensing courses"},{"text":"Watershed management training"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Before you enrol","text":"Check the current syllabus, fees and eligibility on the certifying body's official website."}]},{"heading":"Higher Education Options in India","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Options after your degree:"},{"type":"lis